  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Main journey (browser drives each step)",
      "items": [
        "Upload → POST /extract per file → 202 with a task_id",
        "Browser polls GET /tasks/{id} every 2 s until SUCCESS or FAILURE",
        "OCR text → POST /translate/text (domain: banking)",
        "Translated text → POST /map with a per-document schema",
        "Mapped fields → POST /cases → PASS / FAIL / NEEDS_REVIEW, saved in one transaction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Async OCR (Celery)",
      "items": [
        "OCR API saves the upload to a temp dir and queues only the file path, not the bytes",
        "One worker (concurrency 1) takes tasks from Redis, runs Surya, and stores the result in Redis",
        "The gateway only reads results; it never queues or runs tasks",
        "The worker writes a heartbeat key every 10 s; OCR /health reads it and refuses uploads if it is missing",
        "Translation, field mapping and cases are still plain request/response"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust boundaries",
      "items": [
        "Only :8080 (gateway) and :5173 (frontend) are published to the host",
        "The gateway has no authentication and allows CORS from any origin",
        "Anyone who knows a task_id can read that OCR result via GET /tasks/{id}",
        "Internal services use 127.0.0.1; Postgres, Redis and Ollama publish no host port",
        "Aadhaar and PAN numbers are Fernet-encrypted in golden_records; OCR text in Redis is not encrypted",
        "Only outbound internet traffic: HuggingFace model downloads (and manual `ollama pull`)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Caveats",
      "items": [
        "Diagram reflects commit 23a6131",
        "Translation and mapping each process one request at a time (asyncio lock)",
        "Timeouts temporarily raised to 1800 s (marked TEMP in code)",
        "Extraction/ (legal-case pipeline) is a separate project and is not shown"
      ]
    }
  ]
